      "text": "To find the value of the given expression $19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2$, we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that $a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)$. Applying this formula to each pair, we get:\n\n\\[\n19^2 - 17^2 = (19 + 17)(19 - 17) = 36 \\cdot 2 = 72\n\\]\n\\[\n15^2 - 13^2 = (15 + 13)(15 - 13) = 28 \\cdot 2 = 56\n\\]\n\\[\n11^2 - 9^2 = (11 + 9)(11 - 9) = 20 \\cdot 2 = 40\n\\]\n\\[\n7^2 - 5^2 = (7 + 5)(7 - 5) = 12 \\cdot 2 = 24\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 - 1^2 = (3 + 1)(3 - 1) = 4 \\cdot 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nNow we sum these results:\n\n\\[\n72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8 = 200\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is \\boxed{200}.",
